---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand, contact } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-09-22';
const title = `Privacy policy — ${brand.name}`;
const description = 'What this website collects (almost nothing), what happens when you open the scheduler or WhatsApp, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy/">
  <section class="page-head on-void">
    <div class="wrap wrap-wide">
      <p class="kicker" data-reveal="up">Privacy</p>
      <h1 data-split>Short, because <em>there is little to tell.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal="up" style="--i:2">
        This is a static website. It has no accounts, no forms that post to a server, no analytics and no advertising
        pixels. Last updated <time datetime={updated}>September 22, 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 data-reveal="up">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        {brand.legalName} (CNPJ {brand.cnpj}), {brand.city}, {brand.country} — “{brand.name}”, “we”. For anything in this
        policy, contact us through the channels on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">What this site collects</h2>
      <ul data-reveal="up">
        <li>
          <strong>Nothing, by default.</strong> The pages are static files. We do not run analytics, tag managers, session
          recording, heat maps or advertising scripts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>One preference in your browser.</strong> If you use the “Motion” toggle in the footer, the choice is saved
          in your browser’s local storage under the key <code>vesta-motion</code>. It never leaves your device and you can
          clear it from your browser settings. It is not a cookie.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is served by a hosting provider (GitHub Pages or a CDN), which may keep
          standard server logs — IP address, user agent, requested page, time — for security and operations, under its
          own policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">When you take an action</h2>
      <ul data-reveal="up">
        <li>
          <strong>Scheduler.</strong> The booking widget (Calendly) loads only after you press “Load the scheduler”. From
          that point Calendly processes the details you enter to book the call, under
          <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Calendly’s privacy policy</a>. We receive
          your name, e-mail, time-zone and any notes you add, and use them only to hold the call and follow up on it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>WhatsApp and LinkedIn.</strong> Those links open the respective apps or websites, which have their own
          policies. Messages you send us there are used only to answer you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Projects.</strong> If we work together, the data needed to deliver the project (contacts, access to your
          tools, invoicing details) is processed under the service agreement, kept for as long as the law requires for
          invoices, and deleted or returned after that.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">Legal basis and your rights</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        For visitors in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom (GDPR / UK GDPR), we process contact data on the
        basis of taking steps at your request before entering a contract, and project data on the basis of the contract
        itself. You may request access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability of your data, or object to
        processing, at any time. You also have the right to complain to your local supervisory authority.
      </p>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        For California residents (CCPA / CPRA): we do not sell or share personal information, and we do not use it for
        targeted advertising. You may request to know what we hold about you and ask for it to be deleted. We will not
        treat you differently for exercising those rights.
      </p>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        For visitors in Brazil (LGPD), the same rights apply, and {brand.legalName} is the controller.
      </p>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">Transfers and retention</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        We are based in Brazil. Contact data you send us is stored in the tools we use to answer you (e-mail, WhatsApp,
        Calendly), which may store it in the United States or the EU under their own safeguards. We keep contact data for
        as long as the conversation is active plus twelve months, and invoicing records for the period Brazilian tax law
        requires.
      </p>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">Changes</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Material changes are noted on this page.
      </p>
      {
        contact.email.confirmed && (
          <p data-reveal="up">
            Questions: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email.address}`}>{contact.email.address}</a>.
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-block: calc(var(--nav-h) + clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 6rem)) clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 3rem);
  }

  .page-head > .wrap > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    background: var(--paper-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
  }
</style>
